WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
A recording can give your attention a place to begin. But what does the evidence actually prove?

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
In one experiment, a suggestion changed how selected volunteers responded to printed words. That wasn't a test of a commercial audio track.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
The historical record of animal magnetism teaches a similar lesson: a witnessed experience doesn't prove its proposed cause.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Before buying a twelve-minute meditation program, try your own free twelve-minute task and keep a simple record.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
If you prefer a structured course, read its real contents, terms, and independent evidence.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Begin with the source, not the promise.
